id: pm-09rdni
title: "GH-840: annotation primitives lack a merge-safe structured event append and query contract"
description: "Add a validated, append-only structured event facet that preserves notes' union-merge safety while providing SDK/CLI/MCP encoding, filtering, and provenance contracts."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T10:41:38.295Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T13:33:40.207Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T12:54:11.001Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T12:54:11.001Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Add a typed public SDK structured-event primitive backed by a union-merged item collection; Expose equivalent CLI and MCP mutation/read contracts with deterministic JSON validation and bounded filtering; Warn in append help that body appends are scalar and direct concurrent agents to the merge-safe event surface; Prove multi-branch merge preservation, malformed-input rejection, projections, and packed-consumer behavior"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: github
severity: medium
environment: "pm-cli 2026.7.29, Node 22, concurrent git branches"
resolution: "Notes provide canonical append-only structured JSON events with SDK, CLI, and MCP parity, deterministic validation, bounded time/type filtering, metadata, and immutable post-append behavior."
expected_result: Agents append validated structured events through one SDK-first contract and query bounded event ranges without parsing free-text notes.
actual_result: "pm append mutates scalar body text and notes accept only free text, forcing ad hoc JSON encoding and full client-side scans."
component: SDK annotations and merge-safe context events
